      {
        "t": "mistake",
        "html": "Reading every <b>per-</b> as “through” a place. In many words it just means “thoroughly” and makes the word stronger: to <i>perturb</i> is to disturb thoroughly, not to disturb through something. And <b>per-</b> is not <b>pre-</b> (before): <i>perspective</i> and <i>prescient</i> start with different prefixes."
      },
      {
        "t": "note",
        "html": "Both <b>transient</b> and <b>transitory</b> come from a Latin verb meaning “to go across” (<i>trans-</i> + <i>ire</i>, to go). A transient visitor is passing through; a transitory feeling passes quickly."
      },
